{"slug":"ops-merge-gates","title":"Merge Gates (Phase 2 onward)","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Why a PR cannot be merged until every gate below is green, and how to run them locally before pushing."}]},{"id":"b2","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Pre-merge gates (as of Phase 2)"},{"id":"b3","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A PR targeting "},{"type":"text","value":"main","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" must clear:"}]},{"id":"b4","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Static audit","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — Reviewer reads the diff for logic, security, and architectural fit. Catches most defects but not all (see lessons-learned below)."}],[{"type":"text","value":"format","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" CI job","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":".github/workflows/elixir.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", runs "},{"type":"text","value":"mix format --check-formatted","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"text","value":"Blocking.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Its own dedicated, fast job (~30s, no DB, no full compile) so an unformatted PR short-circuits before the heavier jobs. Split out of "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" because that job is advisory."}],[{"type":"text","value":"mix-prod-compile","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" CI job","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — same workflow, depends on "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Cleans "},{"type":"text","value":"api/_build/prod","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", force-recompiles deps, then runs "},{"type":"text","value":"MIX_ENV=prod mix compile --warnings-as-errors","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"text","value":"This is the gate.","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"validation-perf","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" CI job","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — same workflow, independent of "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Runs the synthetic 200-field / 100-rule bench, takes the median of 5 timed runs, fails if the median exceeds 100ms. "},{"type":"text","value":"Blocking","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — a perf regression blocks merge even while the test suite is advisory."}],[{"type":"text","value":"plugin-node","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" CI job","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":".github/workflows/plugin-node.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Discovers plugins under "},{"type":"text","value":"api/priv/plugins/","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" whose "},{"type":"text","value":"plugin.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" declares a top-level "},{"type":"text","value":"\"node\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" object and runs "},{"type":"text","value":"npm ci","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" + lint + typecheck per plugin. Emits a no-op success when no plugin declares Node, so the workflow is always present in the required-status list."}]]},{"id":"b5","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-test","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" CI job","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":".github/workflows/elixir.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") — dev-mode "},{"type":"text","value":"mix compile --warnings-as-errors","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"text","value":"mix test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" against Postgres — is "},{"type":"text","value":"advisory","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"continue-on-error: true","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") while pre-existing test-infra drift is remediated. It cannot block merge in its current state; once the fix groups land, drop "},{"type":"text","value":"continue-on-error","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to make it blocking again."}]},{"id":"b6","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The branch protection on "},{"type":"text","value":"main","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" requires the "},{"type":"text","value":"format","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-prod-compile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" gates (plus "},{"type":"text","value":"validation-perf","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") to be green. "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is advisory. "},{"type":"text","value":"plugin-node","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is required only when the PR touches "},{"type":"text","value":"api/priv/plugins/**","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b7","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Local pre-merge check"},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Run this before pushing — it mirrors the CI gate exactly:"}]},{"id":"b9","type":"code","value":"make precheck\n# or, equivalently:\ncd api && rm -rf _build/prod && MIX_ENV=prod mix deps.get && \\\n  MIX_ENV=prod mix deps.compile --force && \\\n  MIX_ENV=prod mix compile --warnings-as-errors"},{"id":"b10","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Why a partial clean is not enough"},{"id":"b11","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"CLAUDE.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" golden rule #1 and \"Past Mistakes\" #1: cleaning only "},{"type":"text","value":"_build/prod/lib/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (or any subset) leaves stale "},{"type":"text","value":".beam","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" artifacts for HEEx templates and dependent modules. The compiler is happy with the existing artifacts and does not re-evaluate the module graph; the bug then surfaces only on the production server after a fresh deploy. "},{"type":"text","value":"Always ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"rm -rf _build/prod","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" first.","marks":["strong"]}]},{"id":"b12","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Why dev-mode mix compile is insufficient"},{"id":"b13","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"MIX_ENV=dev","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" enables compile-time leniency that "},{"type":"text","value":":prod","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" does not — most notably, certain macro-vs-function ambiguities in "},{"type":"text","value":"runtime.exs","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"when","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" guards. "},{"type":"text","value":"mix test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" runs under "},{"type":"text","value":":test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and is similarly lenient. Only "},{"type":"text","value":"MIX_ENV=prod mix compile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" exercises the prod compiler; only the prod compiler rejects the PR #42 bug class."}]},{"id":"b14","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Lessons-learned: PR #42 macro-in-guard (2026-04-25)"},{"id":"b15","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"PR #42 (Phase 1 — Oban + plugin_settings + Cloak encryption) introduced a "},{"type":"text","value":"when","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"-guard in "},{"type":"text","value":"config/runtime.exs","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" that referenced a macro instead of a plain function. The construct compiled cleanly under "},{"type":"text","value":":dev","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":":test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", the test suite passed, and the Reviewer's static audit did not flag it. The defect surfaced only on the production server during the rebuild that followed merge: "},{"type":"text","value":"MIX_ENV=prod mix compile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" failed, the systemd service failed to restart, and PR #43 ("},{"type":"text","value":"be53a98 fix(api): move config_env() out of when-guard","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") was filed the same day as a hotfix."}]},{"id":"b16","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"What the new gate catches:"}]},{"id":"b17","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Macro-vs-function misuse in ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"when","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"-guards","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" that the prod compiler rejects but "},{"type":"text","value":":dev","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":":test","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" accept."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Missing or stale ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"_build/prod","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" artifacts","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" that a partial clean would hide on a developer's machine."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Forgotten ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"--warnings-as-errors","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" drift","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" across config branches."}]]},{"id":"b18","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"What it does "},{"type":"text","value":"not","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" catch (still requires Reviewer + tests):"}]},{"id":"b19","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Logic errors that compile cleanly in every environment."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Schema/data migrations that compile but fail at runtime."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Anything that requires the database, the BEAM runtime, or external services to be active."}]]},{"id":"b20","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"When to override"},{"id":"b21","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"text","value":"mix-prod-compile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" gate may be bypassed only by an explicit Boss decision "},{"type":"text","value":"recorded as a task in the task system","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (dogfood it — the task "},{"type":"text","value":"is","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" the durable decision record; do not write to "},{"type":"text","value":".doey/plans/","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", that directory was archived to "},{"type":"text","value":"_attic","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Capture the reason and the follow-up to remove the override on the task itself:"}]},{"id":"b22","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A task is a "},{"type":"text","value":"type:\"task\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" document created through the standard mutate endpoint ("},{"type":"text","value":"content.kind","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" must equal "},{"type":"text","value":"\"task\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"); there is no bespoke "},{"type":"text","value":"POST /v1/tasks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" create verb — the "},{"type":"text","value":"bp task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" verbs are read/lifecycle only ("},{"type":"text","value":"ls","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"ready","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"get","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"close","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"id":"b23","type":"code","value":"TOKEN=barkpark-dev-token\n\n# 1. Record the override decision as a task. Pick a stable doc id (<task_id>).\ncurl -sS -X POST http://localhost:4000/v1/data/mutate/production \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"mutations\":[{\"create\":{\n        \"_id\": \"merge-gate-override-<pr>\",\n        \"_type\": \"task\",\n        \"title\": \"merge-gate override: mix-prod-compile bypassed for <PR #>\",\n        \"content\": {\n          \"kind\": \"task\",\n          \"lifecycle_status\": \"open\",\n          \"decision\": \"Boss approved bypassing the mix-prod-compile gate.\",\n          \"reason\": \"<why>\",\n          \"follow_up\": \"<remove the override: what + when>\",\n          \"merge_sha\": \"<sha>\",\n          \"labels\": [\"merge-gate-override\", \"ops\"]\n        }\n      }}]}'\n# → the create lands as drafts.merge-gate-override-<pr>; the doc id you chose\n#   is <task_id> below."},{"id":"b24","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Optionally attach a written paper (a Bulldocs paper the task references) when the rationale needs prose longer than a task body — author it through the Bulldocs ingest API, then link it:"}]},{"id":"b25","type":"code","value":"curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:4000/v1/tasks/<task_id>/papers \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"add\": [\"merge-gate-override-<pr>\"]}'"},{"id":"b26","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Any merge that lands without the gate green must be reverted within 24h unless that override task exists."}]},{"id":"b27","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Documentation review rules (doc-gates)"},{"id":"b28","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"PRs touching "},{"type":"text","value":"*.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" also run "},{"type":"text","value":".github/workflows/doc-gates.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":"scripts/check-doc-budgets.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (byte caps + 7-card cap) and "},{"type":"text","value":"scripts/docs-anchors-check.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (routing/INDEX targets, card Code anchors, G1 doc-tier headers, canonical-for uniqueness, ARCHIVED banners). Both are "},{"type":"text","value":"blocking","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":". Reviewer rules on top of the scripts:"}]},{"id":"b29","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"a. A new top-level feature requires a routing-table row or a card update in the "},{"type":"text","value":"same PR","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"b. A new card requires retiring or merging one (G2 — hard cap at 7 cards; enforced as a count in "},{"type":"text","value":"check-doc-budgets.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")."}],[{"type":"text","value":"c. A PR touching a file that a card anchors must update the card, or the anchor check fails."}],[{"type":"text","value":"d. Golden Rules and Past Mistakes in root "},{"type":"text","value":"CLAUDE.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" are verbatim-exempt — any edit to them requires explicit owner sign-off."}],[{"type":"text","value":"e. "},{"type":"text","value":"_attic/","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is append-only; restoring a doc is a "},{"type":"text","value":"git mv","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" back plus a MANIFEST note."}]]},{"id":"b30","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"On byte-cap overflow: split to the owning contract/runbook or retire content — never raise the cap."}]},{"id":"b31","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Quick reference"},{"id":"b32","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Need to do"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Command"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Run the gate locally"}],[{"type":"text","value":"make precheck","marks":["code"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Run the dev test suite"}],[{"type":"text","value":"cd api && mix test","marks":["code"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Run the plugin matrix test"}],[{"type":"text","value":"bash api/test/scripts/test-plugin-node-matrix.sh","marks":["code"]}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Lint the workflows"}],[{"type":"text","value":"actionlint .github/workflows/*.yml","marks":["code"]}]]]},{"id":"b33","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"actionlint","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is not installed by default in this repo's environment. To add it locally: "},{"type":"text","value":"brew install actionlint","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (macOS) or "},{"type":"text","value":"go install github.com/rhysd/actionlint/cmd/actionlint@latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". CI does not currently run "},{"type":"text","value":"actionlint","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; add it as a separate workflow if drift becomes common."}]}],"related":[]}
